data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Now I understand the full picture. The mission (from mission.md):\n\n- Deliver `src/greet.py` with `greet(name)` returning `\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\"` and `tests/test_greet.py` covering a normal name and the empty string, with `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exiting 0.\n- All three satisfied is met.\n\nMy loop:\n1. Plan the work.\n2. Dispatch to dev with everything it needs.\n3. Wait.\n4. Judge the reply — fetch the branch, check the actual code and run the tests myself.\n5. Accept or send rework.\n6. Reply to m1 with the outcome.\n\nLet me set up a todo list, then record a plan note, then send the dispatch to dev.\n\nFirst, let me look at my own subject repo briefly to understand what's there (I'm not writing code, but understanding the repo state helps me write a good dispatch and judge later). Actually — the orientation says I have my own clone at ~/subject. The dev has its own clone. Let me check the repo structure quickly.\n\nLet me plan:\n1. Note plan\n2. Send dispatch to dev\n3. Wait\n4. Judge (fetch branch, verify files + run tests)\n5. Accept or rework\n6. Reply to m1\n\nLet me check the subject repo first."},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1787461591,"id":"chatcmpl-2995af7ba2a94feb84a691805adb1669","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

